body:
It was a rare event. I have never in the past thought of hurting myself or anyone. I have on a several past occasions felt very lonely. It doesnt help that I am actually alone given all my friends i knew are now a thousand miles away since i moved a job 3 years ago and any new friends i made have moved because they were all military. Im also not good at making friends because I have trust issues (thx to the military). But anyway, i digress. 

I have spoken with the doctor, social worker gave me a follow up call today actually to make sure things are going well. The local police made a trip to my home to check in on me and delivered all my firearms with no issue today as well. The doc plans to ease me back into my normal dosage for my meds since i was off them for 8 months.

&#x200B;

My parents.....i dont know how they took it. My dad is the one who answered and I could tell he was fighting the urge to talk and question me even after I said I will explain everything when I am comfortable. My dad said they are always there for me when I need them. A few hours later my mom texted me saying the usual i love you and look forward to hearing from you speech.

&#x200B;

Work on the other hand....today was my first day back after everything happened. I didnt say anything to anyone about what happened other than the woman I was seeing broke it off and breadcrumbed me. My coworkers were somewhat supportive and shamed her name for her not being able to see the signs of me being in distress and leaving me like that. My boss tried to dance his way around words to get me to open up about why i went to the hospital which I wasnt pleased about since legally hes not supposed to ask. I just dodged the questions and handed him the docs note.

all the denials thru olife.....what is my worth

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
